  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> produced when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>131</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> of cyclohexane carbaldehyde undergoes Tollen&rsquo;s test is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi></math>. (Nearest Integer)</p><p>Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "60",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RCHO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Ag</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>OH</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>RCOONH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RCHO</mi></math>&nbsp;is cyclohexane carbaldehyde (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></math>). The molar mass is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>112</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>.</p><p>The number of moles of cyclohexane carbaldehyde<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>131</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mn>112</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>176</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of aldehyde produces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>176</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;mol aldehyde will produce</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>176</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> produced <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>176</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>17</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>59</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>97</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8776;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math></p>",
